#% title
# count_distinct_by

#% text
# `count_distinct_by(xs, f)` gives the number of distinct values of `f(x)` over the elements of `xs` (the values of an association). `count_distinct_by(f)(xs)` is the operator form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
count_distinct_by([[a, x], [a, y], [b, z]], first)
#% output
#= 2

#% cell
count_distinct_by([1, 2, 3, -2, -3], abs)
#% output
#= 3

